Test frames — tracked in git.

Real captures from the rig, undistorted with the calibration in force
(Configuration/Calibration_<Hardware>.yaml) and shot at the camera window the
configuration sets, so they are comparable with the empty-surface reference in
Data/Images/Background/. The frames are Image_NNN.png directly in this directory.

The configuration's Evaluation.Frames names this directory as the pinned test set:
Example/Vision/analyze.py runs it, and the tests' expected object counts refer to it
by frame name. A frame's name is only meaningful inside that set — renumbering,
adding or moving frames changes what the pins test, so update them in the same change.
A name once used is never given to another image: 001-013 belonged to the previous
set (All/, recoverable from git commit 1061966), so this set starts at 014.

NOT MET by the current frames (Image_014-054): they carry no undistortion border, so they
did not go through the application's undistortion with the calibration in force. See
KNOWN_ISSUES.md, "Nine frames count one extra object against the old reference".
